23:T82b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use PPF Calculator","description":"The Public Provident Fund (PPF) is a government-backed long-term savings scheme with a 15-year lock-in, tax-free interest and a deduction on contributions under the old tax regime. This PPF calculator estimates your maturity value from a yearly deposit, an assumed interest rate and the number of yea","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/ppf-calculator","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"PPF Calculator"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to use the PPF calculator","text":"Enter the amount you will deposit each year, the current PPF interest rate and the number of years. The default rate in the tool matches the recent government rate, but the government reviews PPF rates every quarter, so check the latest announcement on the India Post or Ministry of Finance site."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Why PPF is popular with Indian savers","text":"PPF follows the EEE model: the contribution qualifies for a deduction under Section 80C in the old regime, the interest is tax-free, and the maturity amount is tax-free. The government guarantees the scheme, so there is no market risk. For conservative investors these features are hard to match."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"How the maturity amount is calculated","text":"This calculator compounds the balance once a year: each year it adds your deposit and then applies the annual rate. It is a clean estimate of the corpus. The real PPF computes interest monthly on the lowest balance between the 5th and month-end, then credits it at the end of the financial year, so the exact figure in your passbook can differ slightly."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Extending PPF beyond 15 years","text":"After 15 years you can close the account, keep it without further deposits and continue to earn interest, or extend it in blocks of five years with or without contributions. Many people extend with contributions to keep building a tax-free retirement fund."}]}21:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$23"}}]
